{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789816735,"nonce":"xt7+iKwTBlSewlZ/EN28WNbNATg=","title":"Cranelift body reads zero for a parameter a loop entry also loads","message":"A function parameter that a loop's OSR entry lists among its externals (the loop reads the parameter and nothing copied it into a local first) is defined for the loop through an OSR variable. The entry block bound the parameter to the Cranelift argument but never defined that variable, so on the normal path the loop header materialised the variable's default, zero, and `i \u003c n` with `n = 0` ended the loop at once.\n\nUntil now the front end always copied a parameter into a local (`v4 = move v1`), and the copy was the external; the copy is still there, but the CSE keys through copies now, so bodies can read the parameter itself. Seen as `step(n)` returning 0 for every call once its baseline was installed (e2e_top_tier_result_speculation_deopts_mid_body).","files":null}]}